.TH "PERCH-SETUP" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-setup \- create the mxRaven domain, listeners, keys, and routes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch setup [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
setup asks mxRaven for a device code, prints the dashboard approval address, and waits for a workspace owner to approve the perch connected application. After approval it provisions a workspace domain, MTA listener, optional submission listener, API keys, inbound route, sending\-domain policy, and optional S3_STORE rule, then writes perch.yaml.
.PP
The access token is held in memory for the setup run only and is never written to the config. Pass \-\-token or set MXRAVEN_API_TOKEN to use a workspace\-scoped API token instead of interactive approval. Listener and S3 secrets are written inline unless you replace them with *_env references.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Approval requires the workspace owner role. The workspace you approve must match \-\-workspace.
.IP \(bu 2
Publish the DNS records printed by the wizard, or pass \-\-wait to wait for verification.
.IP \(bu 2
Use \-\-no\-browser when the command runs over SSH or as a service user.
.IP \(bu 2
Use \-\-no\-submission for inbound\-only deployments.
.IP \(bu 2
Rate\-limit and policy flags map directly to mxRaven listener settings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir <value>
data directory
.TP
.B \-\-hostname <value>
server hostname
.TP
.B \-\-token <value>
control\-plane bearer token for non\-interactive use (otherwise approve perch in the browser)
.TP
.B \-\-issuer <value>
mxRaven identity issuer URL (default: "https://id.mxraven.com")
.TP
.B \-\-dashboard\-url <value>
mxRaven dashboard URL used for connected\-app approval (default: "https://app.mxraven.com")
.TP
.B \-\-client\-id <value>
connected\-app client ID (defaults to the registered perch client)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-browser
print the approval URL without opening a browser
.TP
.B \-\-base\-url <value>
control\-plane base URL
.TP
.B \-\-workspace <value>
mxRaven workspace slug
.TP
.B \-\-domain <value>
mail domain
.TP
.B \-\-inbound\-domain <value>
inbound domain (defaults to \-\-domain)
.TP
.B \-\-sending\-domain <value>
sending domain (defaults to \-\-domain)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-submission
do not create a submission listener
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-policy <value>
MTA auth policy: none, reject\-dmarc\-fail, reject\-spf\-fail, reject\-unauthenticated (default: "none")
.TP
.B \-\-rspamd
enable Rspamd scanning on the MTA listener
.TP
.B \-\-reject\-malware
reject messages with malware verdicts
.TP
.B \-\-reject\-high\-confidence\-spam
reject messages with spam score >= 10
.TP
.B \-\-mta\-message\-rate <value>
MTA messages per minute (0 leaves default) (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-mta\-recipient\-rate <value>
MTA recipients per minute (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-mta\-task\-rate <value>
MTA tasks per minute (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-mta\-burst <value>
MTA rate\-limit burst (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-mta\-concurrency <value>
MTA max concurrency (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
print planned operations without calling mxRaven
.TP
.B \-\-force
overwrite an existing configuration
.TP
.B \-\-wait
wait for mxRaven DNS verification after setup
.TP
.B \-\-wait\-timeout <value>
DNS verification timeout (default: 10m0s)
.TP
.B \-\-wait\-interval <value>
DNS verification poll interval (default: 15s)
.TP
.B \-\-storage <value>
storage mode: sqlite or s3 (default: "sqlite")
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-endpoint <value>
S3 endpoint URL
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-region <value>
S3 region
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-bucket <value>
S3 bucket
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-prefix <value>
S3 key prefix (default: "perch/")
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-access\-key <value>
S3 access key
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-secret\-key <value>
S3 secret key
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-path\-style
use path\-style S3 addressing
.TP
.B \-\-s3\-key\-template <value>
S3 object key template (defaults to prefix + mailbox.address)
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-cert <value>
TLS certificate file
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-key <value>
TLS private key file
.TP
.B \-\-acme\-email <value>
Let's Encrypt account email
.TP
.B \-\-acme\-domain <value>
comma\-separated ACME domains
.TP
.B \-\-public
bind standard public ports (143/993/587/465)
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch setup \-\-config /etc/perch/perch.yaml \-\-data\-dir /var/lib/perch \\
  \-\-workspace my\-workspace \-\-domain example.com \-\-hostname mail.example.com

perch setup ... \-\-no\-browser

perch setup ... \-\-storage s3 \-\-s3\-bucket my\-mail\-archive \-\-s3\-region auto \\
  \-\-s3\-endpoint https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com \-\-s3\-access\-key <key>

perch setup ... \-\-public \-\-acme\-email admin@example.com \-\-acme\-domain mail.example.com
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_API_TOKEN
legacy control\-plane token for non\-interactive setup
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_ISSUER
mxRaven identity issuer URL
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_DASHBOARD_URL
mxRaven dashboard URL used for approval
.TP
.B MXRAVEN_CLIENT_ID
registered perch connected\-app client ID
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1)
